| Current          | Next                 |
| ---------------- | -------------------- |
| PENDING          | CONFIRMED, CANCELLED |
| CONFIRMED        | PROCESSING           |
| PROCESSING       | PACKED               |
| PACKED           | SHIPPED              |
| SHIPPED          | OUT_FOR_DELIVERY     |
| OUT_FOR_DELIVERY | DELIVERED            |
| DELIVERED        | RETURN_REQUESTED     |
| RETURN_REQUESTED | RETURNED             |
| RETURNED         | REFUNDED             |


Not allowed:

SHIPPED → CANCELLED
DELIVERED → CANCELLED
REFUNDED → SHIPPED
RETURNED → PROCESSING

These validations will be enforced inside OrderServiceImpl.





Why this enum?

Many tutorials only define:

PENDING
SHIPPED
DELIVERED
CANCELLED

That is insufficient for a production system because:

Warehouse needs PROCESSING
Packing team needs PACKED
Delivery partner needs OUT_FOR_DELIVERY
Customer support needs RETURN_REQUESTED
Finance needs REFUNDED

This lifecycle supports realistic order fulfillment.